# Template for the MCP server's bearer token.
#
# deploy/install.sh writes the real file to
# $DATA_DIR/config/victoriametrics-mcp/token.env (mode 600): it reuses the
# token the running container already uses, or generates one, then never
# touches it again. This example is the only token-shaped thing in the repo
# and carries no secret.
#
# Clients must send the same value in the Authorization header:
#   Authorization: Bearer <token>
#
# This token is the whole boundary around the metrics history: every service
# name, scrape address and version the labels carry is readable through it,
# and the store's own API has no authentication. Rotate it with
# `scripts/rotate.sh token:victoriametrics-mcp` if it leaks.
METRICS_MCP_TOKEN=change-me
